//===- SBFAnchorNames.def - Anchor name recovery dictionary -----*- C++ -*-===//
//
// NeverD Decompiler
//
// This file intentionally has no include guard.
//
// SBF_ANCHOR_NAME(NAMESPACE, NAME)
//
// Anchor discriminators are a one-way SHA-256 truncation, so a name can only be
// recovered by hashing candidates and comparing. This is the candidate
// dictionary of names that recur across deployed Solana programs.
//
// A hit is strong evidence rather than a guess: an eight-byte SHA-256 prefix
// collision between two short ASCII names does not occur by accident. A miss
// means only that the name is not in this dictionary, so recovery still reports
// the raw discriminator. Supplying the program's IDL always takes precedence.
//
// Instruction and state names are snake_case, account and event names are
// PascalCase, matching how the Anchor macros derive them from Rust items.
//
// The bulk of the instruction names were adopted from the dictionary published
// with `solana-data-reverser`, but none of its hashes were taken on trust: an
// entry is listed here only when NeverD's own derivation reproduces the
// discriminator that file records for it, and the entries whose stated hash
// did not reproduce were dropped rather than corrected. SBFAnchorTests
// re-derives the whole table and requires it to stay injective, so a name that
// stopped hashing to a distinct value would fail the build's tests rather than
// silently rename a recovered instruction.
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

#ifndef SBF_ANCHOR_NAME
#define SBF_ANCHOR_NAME(NAMESPACE, NAME)
#endif

